{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nContainer plan-review attestations inherit direct live children file-impact declarations. The current binary rule treats every child with an empty path list as undeclared, so a truthful `none` child poisons sibling path declarations and forces whole-HEAD invalidation. Stories 1934, 749c, and 1fd4 established authenticated tri-state scope and the manifest classifier. This story makes container inheritance and P9 consume that contract.\n\n## Behavioral contract\n- Closed children are ignored.\n- A live `paths` child contributes its declared paths.\n- A live `none` child is neutral: it contributes no paths and does not poison siblings.\n- Any live `undeclared` child poisons child inheritance: no child paths are inherited and the container is not classified all-none.\n- `all_none` is true only when at least one live child exists and every live child is authenticated `none`; no live children yields false.\n- Scope precedence is exact: any own, cited, or inherited dependency path yields `paths`; otherwise explicit parent `none` yields `none`; otherwise all-live-children-none promotes only an `undeclared` parent to `none`; otherwise the result is `unscoped`. A parent declared `paths` is never promoted to `none`.\n- P9 passes a leaf declared `none`; for containers it ignores closed children and counts only live `undeclared` children as poisoners. Its advisory names poisoners and offers both path declaration and `--none` as truthful remedies.\n\n## Implementation plan\n1. In `manifest.py`, replace the set-only child helper with a frozen private result containing `paths: frozenset[str]` and `all_none: bool`. No `effective` field is needed because consumers distinguish every required state with those two values. Preserve the poison rule above.\n2. Let `dependency_hashes` accept an optional precomputed child-impact result while preserving its `dict[str, str]` return contract. If absent it computes the result for existing callers; if supplied it adds only the supplied child paths.\n3. In `attest.py::sign_plan_review`, compute child impact once from the supplied full child states. Use the same result for dependency hashing and `container_all_none` classification, with the precedence above. The normal review path already supplies `ctx.children`; `orchestrator.py` needs no edit because `_reads.show_ticket` already returns `file_impact_scope`.\n4. In `resign.py`, preserve the same behavior without network reads: build the full direct-child list from `initial_generation.relation_snapshot.child_ids` and `ticket_states_by_id`, then pass it to `sign_plan_review` inside the existing attested read session. Missing or inconsistent snapshot child state remains a structured refusal, never a broader or falsely narrow signature.\n5. In `det_lint.py`, derive leaf and container P9 outcomes from authenticated `file_impact_scope`, using the same live/closed and neutral/poison rules.\n\n## Behavior-first test design\nTests assert signed manifest dependencies and scope, validity after real file changes, public resign results, and P9 result contracts. They do not inspect source text, private dataclass shape, helper call counts, or implementation names.\n\n- Extend `tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py` with signed-manifest/validity cases: paths+none inherits only path files and survives unrelated drift; a declared child-file change invalidates it; all-none plus undeclared parent signs `none`; explicit parent `none` remains `none`; own parent paths plus all-none remains `paths`; no live children does not synthesize `none`; a live undeclared child keeps child inheritance poisoned/unscoped.\n- Extend `tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py` through `resign_plan_review` to prove cheap resign signs the same child-derived dependency scope as normal signing without a fetch.\n- Extend `tests/unit/test_plan_review.py` P9 cases for a `none` leaf, mixed paths+none container, all-none container, closed undeclared child, and live undeclared poisoner with the `--none` remedy.\n- RED command: `pytest tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py tests/unit/test_plan_review.py -q`. Confirm failures are missing tri-state behavior, not imports or source-text checks.\n- Mutation proof: temporarily restore the legacy behavior that treats live `none` as undeclared, run `pytest tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py tests/unit/test_plan_review.py -q`, and require the mixed-scope manifest/validity, resign, and P9 cases to fail; restore production behavior afterward.\n- Refactoring litmus: a rename or extraction of the private child-impact helper must leave all assertions unchanged because they observe only manifest, validity, resign, and P9 contracts.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Mixed live `paths` and `none` children sign only the path child dependencies.\n- [ ] Mixed-scope signatures survive unrelated file drift.\n- [ ] Mixed-scope signatures become stale when a declared child path changes.\n- [ ] All live children declared `none` promote an undeclared parent to signed scope `none`.\n- [ ] Explicit parent `none` remains signed scope `none`.\n- [ ] Parent-owned paths take precedence over all-none children and remain `paths`.\n- [ ] No live children do not synthesize all-none scope.\n- [ ] Any live undeclared child poisons child inheritance and preserves conservative unscoped fallback when no parent or citation paths exist.\n- [ ] Cheap resign preserves the same child-derived signed scope using its immutable relation snapshot.\n- [ ] P9 passes declared-none leaves and containers whose live children are all declared.\n- [ ] P9 advises only live undeclared children and names both path and `--none` remedies.\n- [ ] The focused contract suite (pytest -q tests/unit/test_attestation_invalidation.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py tests/unit/test_plan_review.py) passes while asserting only observable manifest dependency/scope, validity, resign-result, and P9 verdict/coaching contracts; it contains no source-text searches or assertions on private object shape.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the full test suite pass."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785259865895046001,"uuid":"bffc6fa9-939a-4600-9bc5-cba8551fbf43"}